@page
@model ReadinessModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Connections"; }
<div class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">AN HONEST VIEW OF READINESS</span><h1>Know what’s connected.</h1><p class="muted">The local workflow is real. External integrations need approved access.</p></div></div>
<div class="readiness-grid"><section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">▦</span><span class="badge closed">Available locally</span><h2>Case workspace</h2><p>Capture, reviewed registration, casework, encrypted supporting files, closure checklists and audit history are stored in your workspace.</p><dl><dt>Application</dt><dd>ASP.NET Core · .NET 10</dd><dt>Database</dt><dd>@Model.Database</dd><dt>Access</dt><dd>Single officer account · owner-scoped records</dd></dl></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">✉</span><span class="badge @(Model.GmailConnected ? "registered" : "draft")">@(Model.GmailConnected ? "Connection saved" : "Not connected")</span><h2>Gmail complaint intake</h2><p>Connect your mailbox with read-only OAuth access. Preview up to five text or HTML emails from a custom complaint label, then confirm their import into the review inbox. Gmail messages are not changed; supported text/PDF attachments are extracted locally, not retained as evidence.</p><a class="text-link" href="/GmailSettings">Configure Gmail →</a></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="badge draft">On-demand collection</span><h2>YouTube and Karnataka news</h2><p>Search video metadata or collect matching headlines and excerpts from public news feeds. Retain source links for local review before preparing cases. News needs no API key; YouTube requires a configured key and quota.</p><a class="text-link" href="/PublicSources">Open YouTube and news intake →</a></section><section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="badge draft">@(Model.XConfigured ? "Configured · check latest search" : "Not configured")</span><h2>X public complaint search</h2><p>Collect up to 10 recent matching public posts per explicit request. Retain source links in the private intake inbox and review local classification hints. X access and credits are required. Facebook and Instagram live collection remain pending.</p><a class="text-link" href="/XSettings">Configure X search →</a></section><section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">✦</span><span class="badge @(Model.AiConnected ? "registered" : "draft")">@(Model.AiConnected ? "Configured · not verified" : "Not connected")</span><h2>AI drafting</h2><p>@(Model.AiConnected ? "Configuration is present. A successful request is required to verify the service. All output needs officer review." : "The current draft uses a structured template. It preserves source text without claiming translation or AI analysis.")</p><p class="muted small">Configure OpenAI in this local pilot, or use deployment environment variables. Do not send citizen data until its processing arrangements are approved.</p><a class="text-link" href="/AiSettings">Configure OpenAI →</a></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">▤</span><span class="badge registered">Local extraction available</span><h2>Document intake</h2><p>Text-only PDFs and UTF-8 files can be extracted locally. Scanned or mixed PDFs use the configured PDF-capable OCR service after consent; review every page before preparing a complaint. PDF parsing runs in a separate process with time and memory checks.</p><p class="muted small">PNG/JPEG and scanned-PDF OCR: @(Model.OcrConfigured ? "configured; accuracy and live provider response are not yet verified" : "not connected"). Files are limited to 8 MB; PDFs to 10 pages and extracted text to 6,000 characters. Files are not retained as evidence attachments.</p></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">◉</span><span class="badge @(Model.SpeechConfigured ? "registered" : "draft")">@(Model.SpeechConfigured ? "Configured · not verified" : "Speech service not connected")</span><h2>Voice intake</h2><p>Browser recording and playback are available locally, with a two-minute recording limit. Uploaded WAV, MP3, WebM or Ogg recordings can be transcribed through a configured service and reviewed before registration.</p><p class="muted small">Recording requires browser microphone permission. Audio is sent to the configured speech service only when transcription is submitted with consent.</p></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">◎</span><span class="badge closed">Available locally</span><h2>Citizen assistance</h2><p>English/Kannada guided filing and service suggestions, plus private local case status using an officer-issued seven-day access code. Guidance uses rules and does not submit a government complaint.</p><a class="text-link" href="/Citizen">Open citizen assistance →</a></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">▥</span><span class="badge closed">Available locally</span><h2>Workspace analytics</h2><p>Filter by period, district and service; compare volumes, current status, recorded closure durations and checklist flags. Fictional samples are excluded by default. Download a filtered CSV without complaint narratives.</p><a class="text-link" href="/Analytics">Open analytics →</a></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">↗</span><span class="badge draft">Not connected</span><h2>IPGRS handoff</h2><p>No complaints or closure decisions are sent to the government portal. Local references are not official IPGRS IDs.</p><ul class="plain-list"><li>API specification and test access</li><li>Authentication and network requirements</li><li>Authoritative department and category codes</li><li>Submission, status and closure contracts</li></ul></section>
<section class="panel connection-detail"><span class="connection-icon">◇</span><span class="badge closurereview">Production work remains</span><h2>Deployment readiness</h2><p>Local safeguards are implemented. This prototype has not been independently security audited or operationally validated.</p><ul class="plain-list"><li>Department-approved hosting and AI processing</li><li>Security audit and remediation</li><li>Managed secrets, database and tested backups</li><li>Kannada evaluation and operational evidence</li></ul></section></div>
<section class="panel coverage-panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">PROBLEM STATEMENT COVERAGE</span><h2>An expanding local build.</h2></div></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Use case</th><th>This version</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>UC-1 · Multilingual drafting</td><td>Kannada/English text and reviewed audio transcripts; local templates; configurable AI drafting</td></tr><tr><td>UC-2 · Categorisation and routing</td><td>AI pilot-service suggestions with source excerpts and officer confirmation; explicit keyword fallback; official category codes pending</td></tr><tr><td>UC-3 · Summarisation</td><td>Source-linked briefing of original, resolution, feedback, recent history and selected supporting documents; local excerpts or validated AI-selected quotations</td></tr><tr><td>UC-4 · Social media capture</td><td>Officer capture and reviewed CSV import into the inbox, source IDs, duplicate flags and draft handoff; on-demand X recent search with credentials; Facebook/Instagram collection and response posting pending</td></tr><tr><td>UC-5 · Field capture</td><td>Responsive text and voice-recording intake; CSV field-report import; offline text/photo/voice capture and retryable synchronisation; voice transcripts need review after reconnecting and require an approved speech service</td></tr><tr><td>UC-6 · OCR and handwriting</td><td>Local text-PDF/UTF-8 extraction; PNG/JPEG and scanned/mixed-PDF OCR require an approved vision/PDF service; complete-page output is checked before review</td></tr><tr><td>UC-7 · Resolution verification</td><td>Encrypted supporting files, integrity checks, rule-based closure checklist and officer approval; no independent evidence verification</td></tr><tr><td>UC-8 · Policy analytics</td><td>Local period/district/service analytics, duration metrics and filtered CSV; no government-wide data</td></tr><tr><td>UC-9 · Citizen assistant</td><td>English/Kannada guided filing and service help; private local status with expiring access codes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
